cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research or teaching, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "CBF-Safe-Steering-Filter: A Provably-Safe Steering Filter"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aghamohammadi"
    given-names: "Saeed"
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Saeedam02/CBF-Safe-Steering-Filter"
url: "https://github.com/Saeedam02/CBF-Safe-Steering-Filter"
abstract: >-
  A visual Python implementation of a second-order High-Order Control Barrier
  Function safety filter that minimally modifies a nominal yaw-rate command by
  solving an exact one-dimensional hard-constrained quadratic program.
keywords:
  - control barrier functions
  - HOCBF
  - autonomous vehicles
  - quadratic programming
  - robotics
  - safety-critical control
